TITLE:: CompressorCurveView
summary:: the transfer curve, on the meters' dB scale
categories:: Libraries>Compressor
related:: Classes/Compressor, Classes/CompressorPanel, Classes/CompressorHistoryView

DESCRIPTION::
Input level along, output level up, both from -60 to +6 dB on FxMeter's ruler
(code::FxMeter.dbToY::), so its lines are the meters' lines and the history's.
The diagonal is what leaves as it came in; the orchid curve is what the gain
computer makes of it - link::Classes/Compressor#*staticGain::, the server's own
arithmetic, makeup left out - with the knee shaded. The threshold is the
horizontal orchid line through the bend, at the same height as in the history,
and its value sits on a chip in the label column.

Live, a blue dot is where the detector is now and how far the gain is from 0 dB
at this moment; the ring on the curve is where the gain is heading, so the dot
trails it by the attack and the release. Over the curve the hero number is the
most the gain moved in the last second. While the pointer is in the view,
dashed lines fan out from the bend for 2, 4, 8 and 20:1.

table::
## drag the line || the threshold, up and down; shift: fine
## double click it || -20 dB
## the wheel on it || 0.5 dB a step; shift: 0.1
## drag the slope past the bend || the ratio: it follows the pointer (shift: fine)
## double click the slope || 4:1
## cmd + drag anywhere || the ratio, up for more (alt or ctrl too)
## a fan's 2 4 8 20 || that ratio, exactly
## the wheel elsewhere || the knee
::

The view keeps itself square-ish: its width follows its height (200 .. 350 px).
It writes its own hints to a hint bar, since a bar's attach would take over the
pointer it follows.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: comp
ARGUMENT:: parent

METHOD:: floorDb
The bottom of the scale, -60.

METHOD:: ratioPerPixel
How much a pixel of a ratio drag multiplies the ratio by, 1.02.

METHOD:: fanRatios
The ratios the fan shows.

METHOD:: thresholdHint
The hint for the threshold line, shared with the history.
ARGUMENT:: comp

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: comp
METHOD:: view
METHOD:: hints
A hint bar to write to.

METHOD:: hoverAction
Called with the view and what is under the pointer - code::\threshold::,
code::\ratio::, code::\fan::, code::\knee:: or nil - so a panel can light the knob's name.

METHOD:: hot
code::\threshold:: or code::\ratio:: thickens that handle (its knob is hovered).

METHOD:: levelsArrived
The panel calls it on every reply.

METHOD:: heroGain
The most gain change of the last second, in dB, signed.

METHOD:: hint
What is under a point of the view, for the hint bar.
ARGUMENT:: x
ARGUMENT:: y

METHOD:: refresh
